# The stack-frame corpus is data read by two test suites, one of which splits
# it on tabs and compares the last column against an exact expected location.
# A CRLF checkout puts a stray \r on the end of every such column, which fails
# every row while looking identical on screen. Both loaders strip it anyway;
# this keeps the file itself from arriving mangled.
*.tsv text eol=lf
